  <div class="size-guide-instructions">
    <h4>How to Measure Your Ring Size at Home</h4>
    <p>Follow these simple steps to find your perfect fit:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Take a ring that currently fits the intended finger comfortably.</li>
      <li>Place the ring flat on a piece of white paper.</li>
      <li><span>Using a very sharp pencil or a fine-tip pen, carefully trace the <strong>inside</strong> circumference of the ring to draw a circle.</span></li>
      <li><span>Take a ruler and measure the diameter of the drawn circle (the straight line perfectly across the center, from one inner edge to the other) in <strong>millimeters (mm)</strong>.</span></li>
      <li><span>Match your measurement to the "Inside Diameter (mm)" column in the table above to find your correct US size.</span></li>
    </ol>
    <p class="tip"><em>Tip: If your measurement falls exactly between two sizes on the chart, we recommend ordering the larger size for a more comfortable fit.</em></p>
